# Qoduck — findings by Qwen 3.8 Flash (self-excluded: undisclosed stealth identity, zero verified benchmarks)

- Source: Qoder (`Qoduck`, curated id `opencode/qoduck`) — Alibaba-linked AI coding product
- Date: 2026-11-09 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`
- **Exclusion note:** this report is saved as `.md.excluded` because **Qoduck is an anonymous stealth route whose underlying model has not been disclosed**, and Qoder publishes **zero benchmark numbers, specs, or a model card** for it. Its own docs say so plainly: *"Qoduck is a stealth model whose identity has yet to be disclosed. Try it on your own tasks to see how it performs. More information will be shared at an appropriate time."* Per `RULES.md` / `tasks/research.md` Rule 9, a findings file with no verified public benchmark for the exact ID is **self-excluded, never fabricated**. Scoring it would require either inventing capability numbers or importing a guessed parent model's results — both prohibited.

## Model card (verified facts only)

- **Name:** Qoduck (`qoduck`)
- **Status:** **LIVE BUT ANONYMOUS.** Surfaced **2026-11-07** (Singapore time) as a stealth model in Qoder International's model picker, with a limited-time daily free allowance. Promotion end date **TBD**; Qoder will bill at the model's published Credit rate once it ends.
- **What it actually is:** undisclosed. Qoder explicitly declines to name the base model ("Don't ask where it came from" in its launch post). Community chatter on r/LocalLLaMA speculates *"maybe Qwen4"*, but that is an **unverified guess** and per the no-reattribution rule is **not** usable as identity or scoring evidence.
- **Provider / access:** **Qoder International** only (IDE model picker); **individual** plans — Free, Pro Trial, Lite, Pro, Pro+, Ultra. **Teams/Enterprise are ineligible and do not see it.** Qoder IDE/JetBrains plugin/CLI do not carry the promotion. No public API endpoint, no OpenRouter/Zen ID, no Hugging Face checkpoint.
- **Release / knowledge:** promotion started **2026-11-07**; no knowledge cutoff disclosed.
- **IDs:** none published (picker name only).
- **Context window:** **not disclosed.** The curated `meta.json` ("128K total") is a **scaffolded placeholder**, corroborated by nothing.
- **Modalities:** **not disclosed.** `meta.json` "Text in/out" is scaffold boilerplate. Qoduck does expose selectable **thinking-intensity levels** ("even at the highest thinking intensity"), which implies a reasoning-capable model but confirms no I/O modality set.
- **Pricing:** credit-based, not per-token. **Standard 0.5× Credit rate**; **0.0× (free)** inside a limited daily allowance that resets each day (paid plans get a larger allowance). **No $/1M token price exists** for this route.
- **Architecture:** none disclosed.

### Raw benchmarks found

Every category: **no verified public score found** — Qoder publishes no evaluation table, no Artificial Analysis row exists for `qoduck` (it is not a public-API model), and there is no independent same-harness reproduction. Reported behavior is qualitative only (high demand; slower responses at peak).

